<title>CANADA: CWB grain sales rise 28.8 pct in 1995/96.</title>
<headline>CWB grain sales rise 28.8 pct in 1995/96.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of western Canadian wheat, durum, feed and malt barley to the world market in crop year 1995/96 (Aug/July) were 28.8 percent higher than the previous year, the Canadian Wheat Board said.</p>
<p>The CWB has exclusive marketing rights to those grains grown in the Prairie region and sold C$5.8 billion-worth in 1995/96 compared to C$4.5 billion in 1994/95, it said.</p>
<p>Canada is traditionally the second largest supplier to the world wheat market after the United States, slightly ahead of the European Union.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
